  "extractionNotes": "Employee father claims maternity benefit for parental leave 2025-01-01..2025-08-12 (224 days = 32 weeks), starting when the child is almost one year old; the child's mother is not insured, so the father may use the parental leave that is not reserved for her. No ZUS decision or note in the file; the grant is assumed from the file classification (granted in the digest), so every expected value is the claim. Rate not printed: parental leave claimed on its own, 70% inferred. Form errors: the father ticked the 'full maternity + parental leave in the first year' declaration (irrelevant here) and wrote the birth date in the hospital-discharge field; the employer ticked maternity instead of parental leave on the Z-3. Leave request to the employer with the mother's statement of non-use; birth date handwritten on the birth extract and on the ZUR. Z-3 salary table: the first row is labelled 2024-12 but sits before 2024-01 and is read as 2023-12. 2024-01 mostly not worked (sickness and other absence codes). Employer reported up to 20 insured (ZUS pays). asOf = the Z-3 application date (latest dated document)."
